# Addresses whose pageviews are not recorded.
#
# Optional. Copy to /etc/nginx/analytics-exclude.conf on the host and fill in;
# with no such file, nothing is excluded and every visit is recorded.
#
# Not to conf.d/ - nginx.conf includes that directory into the http context,
# where these lines are a syntax error. Not into this repository either: an
# exclusion list describes whoever is running the site rather than the site.
#
# One CIDR (or bare address) per line, value 1 to exclude:
#
#     198.51.100.0/24 1;
#     2001:db8::/32 1;
#
# Use the range the ISP announces rather than the address currently held: a
# consumer address moves around its pool, and an exclusion pinned to one address
# stops working the next time it changes. RDAP gives the allocation:
#
#     curl -sL https://rdap.org/ip/<address>
#
# Two things worth weighing before adding a range:
#
#   - An ISP allocation covers every subscriber on it. Excluding one also
#     discards genuine visitors who share it, so the site goes blind to them.
#     Often the right trade for a small site, but it is a trade.
#   - A shared VPN exit range is the wrong thing to put here. Those addresses
#     have strangers behind them, and #toggle-goatcounter already covers the
#     same browser wherever it connects from.
#
# After editing: sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
#
# To check a decision took effect, from the network in question:
#
#     curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' \
#         'https://playground.ghul.dev/stats/count?p=/exclusion-test'
#
# 202 means excluded and not recorded; 200 means it was counted.
